libmbd
------------------------------------------
Libmbd implements the many-body dispersion (MBD) method in several programming
languages and frameworks.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libgfortran5-14.4.0-1
  liblapack0-3.12.0-1
  libmbd-devel-0.16.0-1bl1
  libmbd0-0.16.0-1bl1
  pkg-config-3.0.11-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.13-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gcc-fortran-14.4.0-1
  liblapack-devel-3.12.0-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/libmbd/libmbd

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/libmbd/libmbd/archive/refs/tags/0.16.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack libmbd-0.16.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./libmbd-0.16.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/libmbd-0.16.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libmbd-0.16.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libmbd0-0.16.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libmbd-devel-0.16.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(libmbd)
